### Delete incomplete staging files even when stream disposal fails

**Severity:** `medium`

`FileStream.Dispose()` can surface a deferred flush or write error. When that happens here, control skips `deleteFile`, leaving an incomplete `.partial` file in the destination directory. Run cleanup from a `finally` block so deletion is still attempted while the original disposal failure continues to propagate.

```suggestion
        try
        {
            Stream.Dispose();
        }
        finally
        {
            if (!completed)
            {
                deleteFile(stagingPath);
            }
        }
```
